<?xml version="1.0"?><iai friendlyname="HIV Life Cycle" id="0000EECA" height="329" width="556" hasaudio="0" hascredits="0" lang="E" basecontroltype="SlideShowControl" outlinecolorid="1" skinstyle="Standard" skinlib="standard"><slides><slide type="standard" sequence="1" slideid="40"><standardslide locklabelson="1" showtextarea="1" useshowhidelabels="0" lockpicon="0" useswfctrl="0" vrslide="0"><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body>&lt;html&gt;Como todos los virus, el virus de la inmunodeficiencia humana (VIH) está formado solamente por material genético, unas pocas proteínas y una cubierta protectora. Su material genético está formado por dos cadenas simples de ARN, que contienen toda la información necesaria para fabricar más virus. El VIH no puede reproducirse fuera de la célula, pero cuando invade una célula viva la convierte en una fábrica dedicada a construir más virus.&lt;/html&gt;</body><title>&lt;html&gt;Virus libre&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><image>T304366-1.swf</image><audiofile/><labels><label labelid="93" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="191" y="11"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;HIV&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;VIH&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="187" y="12" w="27" h="15"/></label><label labelid="94" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="148" y="99"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;Viral proteins&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Proteínas virales&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="144" y="100" w="90" h="15"/></label><label labelid="95" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="189" y="35"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;RNA&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;ARN&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="185" y="36" w="30" h="15"/></label><label labelid="96" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="191" y="162"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;Cell&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Célula&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="187" y="163" w="39" h="15"/></label></labels><keywords/><imagerefid/><audiorefid/><imageheight>308</imageheight><imagewidth>400</imagewidth><listtitle>&lt;html&gt;Virus libre&lt;/html&gt;</listtitle><hidelbltext>&lt;html&gt;Ocultar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</hidelbltext><showlbltext>&lt;html&gt;Mostrar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</showlbltext></standardslide></slide><slide type="standard" sequence="2" slideid="41"><standardslide locklabelson="1" showtextarea="1" useshowhidelabels="0" lockpicon="0" useswfctrl="0" vrslide="0"><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body>&lt;html&gt;El VIH se une a receptores específicos de la superficie celular. Estos receptores solo se encuentran en algunos tipos de células, entre las que se incluyen algunos leucocitos, células intestinales y células cerebrales.&lt;/html&gt;</body><title>&lt;html&gt;El VIH se une a la célula&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><image>T304366-2.swf</image><audiofile/><labels><label labelid="100" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="26" y="28"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;CD4 Receptor&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Receptor CD4&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="22" y="29" w="77" h="15"/></label><label labelid="101" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="172" y="168"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;Co-Receptor&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Co-receptor&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="168" y="169" w="63" h="15"/></label><label labelid="128" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="192" y="11"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;HIV&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;VIH&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="188" y="12" w="27" h="15"/></label><label labelid="241" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="232" y="287"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;Cell&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Célula&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="228" y="288" w="39" h="15"/></label></labels><keywords/><imagerefid/><audiorefid/><imageheight>308</imageheight><imagewidth>400</imagewidth><listtitle>&lt;html&gt;El VIH se une a la célula&lt;/html&gt;</listtitle><hidelbltext>&lt;html&gt;Ocultar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</hidelbltext><showlbltext>&lt;html&gt;Mostrar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</showlbltext></standardslide></slide><slide type="standard" sequence="3" slideid="42"><standardslide locklabelson="1" showtextarea="1" useshowhidelabels="0" lockpicon="0" useswfctrl="0" vrslide="0"><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body>&lt;html&gt;A continuación, la envuelta vírica se funde con la membrana plasmática y el VIH libera su contenido en el interior de la célula huésped.&lt;/html&gt;</body><title>&lt;html&gt;El VIH infecta a la célula&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><image>T304366-3.swf</image><audiofile/><labels><label labelid="126" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="179" y="137"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;RNA&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;ARN&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="175" y="138" w="30" h="15"/></label><label labelid="127" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="179" y="164"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;Viral proteins&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Proteínas virales&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="175" y="165" w="90" h="15"/></label></labels><keywords/><imagerefid/><audiorefid/><imageheight>308</imageheight><imagewidth>400</imagewidth><listtitle>&lt;html&gt;El VIH infecta a la célula&lt;/html&gt;</listtitle><hidelbltext>&lt;html&gt;Ocultar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</hidelbltext><showlbltext>&lt;html&gt;Mostrar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</showlbltext></standardslide></slide><slide type="standard" sequence="4" slideid="50"><standardslide locklabelson="1" showtextarea="1" useshowhidelabels="0" lockpicon="0" useswfctrl="0" vrslide="0"><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body>&lt;html&gt;Una proteína viral, la enzima transcriptasa inversa, transforma las cadenas simples de ARN viral en ADN de doble cadena.&lt;/html&gt;</body><title>&lt;html&gt;El ARN viral se convierte en ADN&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><image>T304366-4.swf</image><audiofile/><labels><label labelid="129" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="163" y="137"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;ADN viral&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;ADN viral&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="159" y="138" w="55" h="15"/></label><label labelid="130" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="163" y="164"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;Transcriptasa inversa&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Transcriptasa inversa&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="159" y="165" w="115" h="15"/></label></labels><keywords/><imagerefid/><audiorefid/><imageheight>308</imageheight><imagewidth>400</imagewidth><listtitle>&lt;html&gt;El ARN viral se convierte en ADN&lt;/html&gt;</listtitle><hidelbltext>&lt;html&gt;Ocultar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</hidelbltext><showlbltext>&lt;html&gt;Mostrar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</showlbltext></standardslide></slide><slide type="standard" sequence="5" slideid="51"><standardslide locklabelson="1" showtextarea="1" useshowhidelabels="0" lockpicon="0" useswfctrl="0" vrslide="0"><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body>&lt;html&gt;El nuevo ADN del virus penetra en el núcleo celular. Otra proteína viral, la enzima integrasa, inserta el ADN viral en el ADN de la célula huésped. La célula es incapaz de distinguir entre el ADN viral y su propio material genético.&lt;/html&gt;</body><title>&lt;html&gt;El ADN viral se inserta en el ADN celular&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><image>T304366-5.swf</image><audiofile/><labels><label labelid="131" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="162" y="137"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title/><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;ADN viral&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="158" y="138" w="55" h="15"/></label><label labelid="132" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="204" y="164"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title/><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Integrasa&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="200" y="165" w="56" h="15"/></label><label labelid="133" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="27" y="83"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title/><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;ADN celular&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="23" y="84" w="67" h="15"/></label><label labelid="134" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="214" y="287"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title/><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Núcleo&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="210" y="288" w="42" h="15"/></label></labels><keywords/><imagerefid/><audiorefid/><imageheight>308</imageheight><imagewidth>400</imagewidth><listtitle>&lt;html&gt;El ADN viral se inserta en el ADN celular&lt;/html&gt;</listtitle><hidelbltext>&lt;html&gt;Ocultar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</hidelbltext><showlbltext>&lt;html&gt;Mostrar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</showlbltext></standardslide></slide><slide type="standard" sequence="6" slideid="52"><standardslide locklabelson="1" showtextarea="1" useshowhidelabels="0" lockpicon="0" useswfctrl="0" vrslide="0"><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body>&lt;html&gt;La célula huésped lleva a cabo las instrucciones codificadas en el ADN viral, haciendo copias del material genómico del virus y de las proteínas virales.&lt;/html&gt;</body><title>&lt;html&gt;Transcripción&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><image>T304366-6.swf</image><audiofile/><labels><label labelid="135" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="119" y="110"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;New viral proteins&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Proteínas virales nuevas&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="115" y="111" w="129" h="15"/></label><label labelid="136" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="222" y="276"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;New viral RNA&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;ARN viral nuevo&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="218" y="277" w="88" h="15"/></label><label labelid="137" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="162" y="137"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;Viral DNA&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;ADN viral&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="158" y="138" w="55" h="15"/></label><label labelid="138" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="27" y="83"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;Cellular DNA&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;ADN celular&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="23" y="84" w="67" h="15"/></label></labels><keywords/><imagerefid/><audiorefid/><imageheight>308</imageheight><imagewidth>400</imagewidth><listtitle>&lt;html&gt;Transcripción&lt;/html&gt;</listtitle><hidelbltext>&lt;html&gt;Ocultar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</hidelbltext><showlbltext>&lt;html&gt;Mostrar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</showlbltext></standardslide></slide><slide type="standard" sequence="7" slideid="53"><standardslide locklabelson="1" showtextarea="1" useshowhidelabels="0" lockpicon="0" useswfctrl="0" vrslide="0"><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body>&lt;html&gt;Una tercera proteína viral, llamada proteasa, divide las cadenas largas de proteínas del VIH en pequeñas proteínas funcionales. Las proteínas virales y el ARN se aproximan en el interior de la célula para facilitar la formación del nuevo virus.&lt;/html&gt;</body><title>&lt;html&gt;Ensamblaje&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><image>T304366-7.swf</image><audiofile/><labels><label labelid="139" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="222" y="214"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;Protease&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Proteasa&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="218" y="215" w="52" h="15"/></label><label labelid="140" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="119" y="110"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;New viral proteins&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Proteínas virales nuevas&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="115" y="111" w="129" h="15"/></label><label labelid="141" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="222" y="246"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;New RNA&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;ARN nuevo&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="218" y="247" w="64" h="15"/></label></labels><keywords/><imagerefid/><audiorefid/><imageheight>308</imageheight><imagewidth>400</imagewidth><listtitle>&lt;html&gt;Ensamblaje&lt;/html&gt;</listtitle><hidelbltext>&lt;html&gt;Ocultar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</hidelbltext><showlbltext>&lt;html&gt;Mostrar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</showlbltext></standardslide></slide><slide type="standard" sequence="8" slideid="54"><standardslide locklabelson="1" showtextarea="1" useshowhidelabels="0" lockpicon="0" useswfctrl="0" vrslide="0"><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body>&lt;html&gt;El ARN y las proteínas virales son “empaquetados” utilizando parte de la membrana de la célula huésped y formando un nuevo VIH, que sale de la célula huésped y puede infectar otras células.&lt;/html&gt;</body><title>&lt;html&gt;Formación de nuevos virus&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><image>T304366-8.swf</image><audiofile/><labels><label labelid="143" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="317" y="248"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;New HIV&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;VIH nuevo&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="313" y="249" w="61" h="15"/></label><label labelid="144" action="static" usepicon="0" useleader="0" textbuttonstyleid="1" usehotarea="0" locklabel="0"><pos x="341" y="137"/><leaderline forecolorid="2" bgcolorid="3"><points/></leaderline><caption titlestyleid="1" bodystyleid="2"><body/><title>&lt;html&gt;Cell&lt;/html&gt;</title><image/><imagerefid/></caption><audiofile/><hotarea/><labeltarget/><picon height="0" width="0" showwireframe="0" showimage="0" colorid="2"><pos x="0" y="0"/><altimage/><altimagerefid/></picon><labeltext>&lt;html&gt;Célula&lt;/html&gt;</labeltext><audiorefid/><bgrct x="337" y="138" w="39" h="15"/></label></labels><keywords/><imagerefid/><audiorefid/><imageheight>308</imageheight><imagewidth>400</imagewidth><listtitle>&lt;html&gt;Formación de nuevos virus&lt;/html&gt;</listtitle><hidelbltext>&lt;html&gt;Ocultar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</hidelbltext><showlbltext>&lt;html&gt;Mostrar etiquetas&lt;/html&gt;</showlbltext></standardslide></slide></slides><slideshowcontrol bottombarbgcolorid="4" textdividerbarcolorid="4" creditsbuttonstyleid="2" resetbuttonstyleid="3" navbuttonstyleid="1" numbermenuitems="1" showpop="1" autoadvance="0" shownavarrows="1" bottombarheight="21"><audiocontrollerstyle bgcolorid="5" progresscolorid="4" guttercolorid="5" graphiccolorid="3" outlinecolorid="2" buttonstyleid="1"/><popmenustyle listtextstyleid="3" displaytextstyleid="3" selectedlisttextstyleid="3" rolllisttextstyleid="3" downlisttextstyleid="3" rolloutlinecolorid="6" displaybgcolorid="3" listbgcolorid="3" listoutlinecolorid="6" displayoutlinecolorid="6" popbuttonstyleid="1"><scrollbarstyle guttercolorid="6" thumbbasecolorid="7" thumbrollcolorid="8" thumbdowncolorid="8" buttonstyleid="1"/></popmenustyle><captionscrollbarstyle guttercolorid="6" thumbbasecolorid="7" thumbrollcolorid="8" thumbdowncolorid="8" buttonstyleid="1"/><creditsbuttontext>&lt;html&gt;Credits&lt;/html&gt;</creditsbuttontext><resetbuttontext>&lt;html&gt;Reset&lt;/html&gt;</resetbuttontext><currentslidetext textstyleid="4"><text>&lt;html&gt;% de #&lt;/html&gt;</text></currentslidetext></slideshowcontrol><textstyles><textstyle size="13" font="Georgia" bold="1" italic="0" underline="0" colorid="2" align="left" 